/**
	Whether the sound system started, with a default audio engine sounds can play on.
	const bool sound_system_available;
	## Remarks:
		Reading this property starts the sound system if it hasn't been started yet. It is false when the default engine can't be built, for example on a machine without an audio output device. Unlike reading `sound_default_engine` or creating a `sound`, which throw an exception in that case, this property never throws, so it is the way to check before playing anything.
		Each read tries again while the sound system isn't available, so it turns true once a device appears. An engine you create yourself with the `AUDIO_ENGINE_NO_DEVICE` flag works either way, and once you assign one to `sound_default_engine` this property reports true.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	if (!sound_system_available) {
		alert("No sound", "The sound system could not start, so this program will run silently.");
		return;
	}
	sound s;
	s.load("ding.ogg");
	s.play_wait();
}
